{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Jethro said</b> — We have found that Zipporah is the daughter of Reuel, for so it is written: <i>and he gave Zipporah his daughter</i>, and furthermore: <i>to water the flock of their father Reuel</i>. Now Hobab is the son of Reuel, so he is the brother of Zipporah. Since the camp was in the wilderness, Chothev is Jethro, because of our encampment in the wilderness, and the verse says concerning Jethro when he came to the wilderness where he was encamped there. If someone objects that the verse says of Jethro <i>Chothev Mosheh</i> (Moses' father-in-law), the answer is that it is the way of Scripture to call the girl's father and her brother both <i>chothen</i>. The proof is <i>Hobab son of Reuel the Midianite, chothen Mosheh</i>, and it has already been established that Hobab was the brother of Zipporah, yet he is called <i>chothen Mosheh</i>. And if one says <i>chothen Mosheh</i> is attached only to Reuel, not to Hobab, the answer is <i>from the sons of Hobab, chothen Mosheh</i>. Many say that Hobab is Jethro, and he is the father of Zipporah, and Reuel was her grandfather, and Scripture says <i>to Reuel their father</i> just as Jacob said <i>the God of my father Abraham</i>, and Scripture says <i>his daughter</i> just as it says of Belshazzar that he is the son of Nebuchadnezzar, when he is his grandson. And our Sages said that Jethro had seven names, and seventy faces to the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:06.624545048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}